Project Lombok is an open-source organization that develops a Java library
designed to reduce boilerplate code in Java applications.
It automatically generates common methods such as getters, setters, constructors,
and builders at compile time through annotation processing, simplifying Java development and improving readability.
Lombok = Java ka shortcut tool for boring code.
Key facts
Founded: 2009
Primary language: Java
License: MIT License
Core tool: Lombok annotation processor (lombok.jar)
Use case: Code generation for repetitive Java constructs

How it works
Lombok leverages the Java Annotation Processing Tool (APT) to modify compiled bytecode.
Developers annotate fields or classes (for example, @Getter, @Setter, or @Builder),
and Lombok injects the corresponding methods during compilation.
This eliminates the need for manually written boilerplate code while maintaining clean, readable source files.

Notable features
Key annotations include:

@Data: Generates getters, setters, toString, equals, and hashCode.

@Builder: Enables the builder design pattern.

@Value: Creates immutable classes.

@Slf4j: Adds logging frameworks seamlessly.
Lombok also provides experimental features like @With and @SneakyThrows for advanced coding patterns.